items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:51:the natural-number power being that of [[def-nat-power]] and the cardinal
items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:52:exponential being defined in ZF here because the function set it counts is
items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:53:finite. Moreover $m \oplus n$ and $m \otimes n$ are also the **ordinal**
items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:54:sum and product of $m$ and $n$ ([[thm-ordinal-arithmetic-agrees-on-omega]]).
items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:55:**No agreement is claimed between the cardinal power and the ordinal power**;
items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:56:[[thm-ordinal-arithmetic-agrees-on-omega]] itself claims none for exponentiation,
items/thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting.md:57:and none is needed below.
