items/cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete.md:36:## Statement
items/cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete.md:37:
items/cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete.md:38:The Cauchy-sequence reals $\mathbb{R}_C$ have the **least-upper-bound property**:
items/cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete.md:39:every nonempty $S \subseteq \mathbb{R}_C$ that is bounded above has a least upper
items/cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete.md:40:bound $\sup S \in \mathbb{R}_C$. Hence, together with [[thm-reals-ordered-field]],
items/cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete.md:41:$\mathbb{R}_C$ is a **complete ordered field** ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
