items/def-real-order.md:26:## Definition
items/def-real-order.md:27:
items/def-real-order.md:28:A real $x$ is **positive** when it has a representative $(a_n)$ together
items/def-real-order.md:29:with a rational $\delta > 0$ and an index $N$ such that $a_n > \delta$
items/def-real-order.md:30:for all $n \ge N$. Define
items/def-real-order.md:31:
items/def-real-order.md:32:$$x \le y \iff x = y \;\text{ or }\; y - x \text{ is positive},$$
items/def-real-order.md:33:
items/def-real-order.md:34:and $|x| = x$ if $x \ge 0$, $|x| = -x$ otherwise.
items/def-real-order.md:35:
items/def-real-numbers.md:28:## Definition
items/def-real-numbers.md:29:
items/def-real-numbers.md:30:The **real numbers** are the quotient ring
items/def-real-numbers.md:31:
items/def-real-numbers.md:32:$$\mathbb{R} := \mathcal{C} / \mathcal{N}$$
items/def-real-numbers.md:33:
items/def-real-numbers.md:34:of the ring of Cauchy sequences ([[thm-cauchy-ring]]) by the ideal of null
items/def-real-numbers.md:35:sequences ([[lem-null-ideal]]). The class of $(a_n)$ is written
items/def-real-numbers.md:36:$[(a_n)]$. Each rational $q$ maps to the class $\hat q$ of the constant
items/def-real-numbers.md:37:sequence $(q, q, q, \dots)$.
