items/def-real-limit.md:25:## Definition
items/def-real-limit.md:26:
items/def-real-limit.md:27:A sequence $(x_k)$ of reals **converges** to $x \in \mathbb{R}$ when for
items/def-real-limit.md:28:every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with
items/def-real-limit.md:29:$|x_k - x| < \hat\varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$. It is **Cauchy** when for
items/def-real-limit.md:30:every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with
items/def-real-limit.md:31:$|x_k - x_l| < \hat\varepsilon$ for all $k, l \ge K$.
items/def-real-limit.md:32:
items/thm-reals-cauchy-complete.md:34:## Statement
items/thm-reals-cauchy-complete.md:35:
items/thm-reals-cauchy-complete.md:36:Every Cauchy sequence of real numbers ([[def-real-limit]]) converges to a real
items/thm-reals-cauchy-complete.md:37:number. Together with [[thm-reals-ordered-field]], this completes the
items/thm-reals-cauchy-complete.md:38:construction: $\mathbb{R}$ is a complete totally ordered field.
items/thm-reals-cauchy-complete.md:39:
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:36:## Statement
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:37:
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:38:Any two complete ordered fields $F$ and $G$ ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]) are
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:39:isomorphic via a **unique** ordered-field isomorphism
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:40:([[def-ordered-field-isomorphism]]) $\varphi : F \to G$, and this $\varphi$
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:41:**fixes $\mathbb{Q}$** ($\varphi \circ \iota_F = \iota_G$). Consequently
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:42:$\mathbb{R}$ is the **unique complete ordered field up to a unique isomorphism**,
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:43:and it admits $\mathbb{Q}$ as an ordered subfield via $\iota_F$.
items/thm-uniqueness-complete-ordered-field.md:44:

