items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:31:## Statement
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:32:
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:33:The map $q \mapsto \hat q$ ([[def-real-numbers]]) is an embedding of ordered
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:34:fields. Every real is approximated by rationals: for $x \in \mathbb{R}$ and
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:35:rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $q \in \mathbb{Q}$ with
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:36:$|x - \hat q| < \hat\varepsilon$. Consequently, strictly between any two
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:37:reals lies a rational.
items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md:38:
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:34:## Statement
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:35:
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:36:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) and let $x, y \in F$, with
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:37:$|x|$ the absolute value ([[def-abs-value]]). Then
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:38:
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:39:$$|x| \ge 0; \quad |x| = 0 \iff x = 0; \quad -|x| \le x \le |x|; \quad |-x| = |x|; \quad |xy| = |x|\,|y|;$$
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:40:
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:41:and, for every $c > 0$, one has $|x| < c \iff -c < x < c$.
items/lem-of-abs-value.md:42:
items/lem-of-add-order.md:33:## Statement
items/lem-of-add-order.md:34:
items/lem-of-add-order.md:35:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) with positive cone $P$, and
items/lem-of-add-order.md:36:let $a, b, c, d \in F$.
items/lem-of-add-order.md:37:
items/lem-of-add-order.md:38:1. **Translation invariance.** If $a < b$ then $a + c < b + c$.
items/lem-of-add-order.md:39:2. **Adding inequalities.** If $a < b$ and $c < d$ then $a + c < b + d$.
